# Gameplay logic

- Damage, targeting, economy, wave, gem, status, and identity rules belong in
  plain C# seams or ScriptableObject data, not in UI views.
- Do not put rules in `Update`, `LateUpdate`, or animation callbacks that read
  `Time` or `UnityEngine.Random`. Pass a clock delta or deterministic RNG into
  the domain service instead.
- Combat ticks use object pools, reused collections, and `for` loops. Do not
  add `System.Linq` to hot combat paths.
- New or changed domain behavior requires a focused EditMode test. Test
  boundaries and invariants rather than copying every authored balance value.
- Keep the dependency direction `UI → Gameplay → Core`; Gameplay must not
  reference UI or Steam.
- Use explicit factories and ScriptableObject data. Do not introduce gameplay
  reflection, attribute scans, or string-to-type registries.
